  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 159 AM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nTemperatures increase into the low 100s for many on Saturday as\nupper level high pressure moves across New Mexico and West Texas.\nRecord or near record temperatures are expected Saturday before\nthe high shifts to the east and cooler air from the gulf is\nadvected into the area next week. Highs beginning Sunday will drop\nslightly into the 90s, cooler than Friday and Saturday but still\nat least 5 degrees above normal for this time of year. Little\nchanges through the rest of the week as high pressure remains\nnearly stationary to our east. There will be a chance for\nafternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms in the higher\nelevations west of the Pecos River, more of a summertime pattern\nthan a fall pattern. We are still looking for our first strong\nfall cold front here. \n\nHennig",
